 This distinction is important because external execution evidence and actual downstream world state can diverge. (Agoragentic)
 
+`COMMITTED` in `ExternalTransaction` and an external commit receipt refer only
+to durability reported by the external system. They MUST NOT be equated with
+`WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT`, which exists only after a successful World Kernel
+atomic commit. An external receipt is evidence for verification, not proof of
+Veda's modeled-World commitment.
+
+The external system supplies only facts it can know and report. Veda MAY keep a
+separate linkage record correlating that evidence with its stable action or
+idempotency identity, candidate transition hash and exact parent World version
+when consequential, evidence-set references, and a VerificationReceipt or
+`WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT` reference when those later records exist. These are
+Veda-owned linkage metadata and MUST NOT be fabricated as provider evidence.
+The original external receipt MUST NOT require a VerificationReceipt reference
+that can exist only after the receipt is observed.
